# Readability review fixes for the Graph Chat / GraphQL / explorer changes

Context: A readability review of the 2026-10-14 Graph Chat performance work
(analyze_graphql, GraphQL fast path, explorer fixes, tracing, KRW formatting)
found four real bugs in the server-side aggregation tool plus code that was
hard to follow: anonymous positional tuples, a 75-line resolver method, prompt
routes lettered out of order, the same id-matching rule written six times,
domain logic in a route and unnamed magic numbers. All changes below are
behaviour-preserving refactors except the bug fixes and the two items marked
"behaviour change".

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/analysis.py
   Bug fixes:
   - fetch_all_rows clamps the effective page limit to MAX_LIST_LIMIT, the
     same clamp the server applies. A query asking for limit 5000 was marked
     complete after the first 1000 rows.
   - Per-list status (LIST_COMPLETE / LIST_ROW_CAP / LIST_PAGE_ERROR)
     replaces the bool, so a failed page is no longer reported as "row cap
     reached". The caller's variables object is passed to the executor
     unchanged.
   - group_rows computes the clamped top once, so the "... more" line is
     shown when top exceeds MAX_TOP. Tie counts come from a Counter.
   - _scalar_matches returns no match for a dict without label/id/uri
     (raised IndexError). "!=" in restrict.compare raised KeyError.
   Readability: EntityRef NamedTuple instead of positional tuples, a _Group
   dataclass and _ranked_lines instead of a dict plus closure, shared _OPS /
   _AGGREGATES tables, restrict split into membership and compare helpers,
   _condition_targets extracted, MAX_HINT_VALUES constant, GraphQLError
   instead of a broad except, AnalysisError now subclasses ValidationError.
2. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/tools.py
   Shared _graphql_executor for query_graphql and analyze_graphql; defaults
   and enum lists come from the analysis constants; argument normalisation
   before the HTTP call; type hints fixed.
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py, .planning/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/SPEC.md
   Prompt routes re-lettered A..H in order (no wording change). The
   describe_entity depth uses a <<DESCRIBE_DEPTH>> placeholder instead of a
   fragile string replace; the default render is unchanged. Stale SPARQL
   mention removed (no SPARQL tool is offered). Named compaction threshold.
4. src/back/core/graphql/ (models, GraphQLSchemaBuilder, SchemaMetadata,
   ResolverFactory, SchemaDigest, constants)
   RelEdge / InverseField / RelTarget / InverseSource NamedTuples;
   _build_entities split into collect / resolve / apply helpers with one
   docstring for the selection semantics; _build_query uses a root-field
   table plus reset_digest() so the digest cannot go stale; FieldFilter
   passed straight through; narrow excepts in selection_tree.
5. src/back/core/graphdb/ (GraphDBBackend, SubjectFilter, SubjectFilterKind
   (new), constants, neo4j/Neo4jReadOps, neo4j/Neo4jStore, lakebase/_companion_ddl)
   Shared _local_id_match_sql / _local_id_match_cypher helpers for the six
   copies of the id-matching rule; relationship-filter SQL built from named
   fragments (note: % and _ in values still act as LIKE wildcards);
   REVERSE_LOOKUP_MAX_ROWS constant; Cypher WHERE built from a small
   structure with explicit spacing and role-named parameters; one index
   table and loop in ensure_graph_indexes. Emitted SQL, Cypher (apart from
   parameter names) and DDL were captured before/after and are identical.
   Behaviour change: an unknown SubjectFilterKind now raises ValidationError
   instead of being treated as a data filter.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py, src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   New DigitalTwin.chat_schema_digest() holds the digest logic (narrow
   excepts, tuple unpacked by name); the router keeps a one-line delegate.
   Named FILTER_* entity constants. Behaviour change: the /sync/filter
   server default for max_entities is 50 (was 5000) to match the UI; the
   explorer always sends the value. _drop_out_of_set_edges uses
   URIHelpers.is_uri.
7. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   LAYOUT_EXTENT / NODE_WAIT_POLL_MS / NODE_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS /
   DEFAULT_MAX_ENTITIES constants; _waitForNode resolves true/false and the
   caller warns on timeout; comments on why seed URIs join the expanded set.
8. src/agents/tracing.py, src/agents/engine_base.py
   _UNTRACED_ARG_NAMES (was _SECRET_ARGS) used by both helpers; trace_llm
   binds arguments by name like trace_tool; comment on the fallback span name.
9. src/agents/tools/graph_formatting.py
   _is_entity_list / _entity_key helpers, math.isfinite, KRW_FIELD_SUFFIX,
   English comments (output strings unchanged).
10. scripts/deploy.sh
   grant_app_self_permissions() shared by step 6c and step 10 (retitled as
   the idempotent backstop); printed messages unchanged.

